      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are describing the terrifying relief of letting go when holding on feels like extending the suffering rather than saving anything. The tragedy of preserving something beautiful through inevitable loss is that it can trap you in an endless ceremony of letting go without giving the feeling closure. While leaving to protect your own peace is a valid and dignifiable choice, remember that this relationship with your past is now entirely up to you, and you hold the power to decide when exactly to draw that final line.",
